<title>KAZAKHSTAN: TABLE-Tajik GDP rises 5.4 pct in Jan-May.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Tajik GDP rises 5.4 pct in Jan-May.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tajikistan's gross domestic product (GDP) grew by 5.4 percent in January-May of this year, compared to the same period last year, the State Statistics Agency said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>    TAJIK GDP			Jan-May 97	    Jan-May 96</p>
<p>    Year-on-year pct change	+5.4		    -20.2</p>
<p>The agency said the growth of GDP despite a fall in industrial production was largely due to the development of the private sector of the economy, particularly of services and trade.</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
